  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want to be notified of new MPs while the app is closed, so that I answer in time.\n\n### Scope\n\nSame BGTask identifier as legacy (update path), LOT-047 poll for the selected account, Keychain readable after first unlock (Q-9), local notification + app icon badge per setting, tap opens the MP list.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: high · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'background MP check scheduling (NET-13)'; FEATURES 'Not to lose': BGTask\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `MPBackgroundService.swift` (BGTask `com.hfrplus.refresh_mp`, notification 'Vous avez un nouveau message privé', app badge), `HFRswift/Info.plist` (`BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers`, `UIBackgroundModes`), `AppSettingsView.swift:528-533`\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-140-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-047 (#73, done)\n- LOT-044 (#70, in-progress)\n- LOT-065 (#90, done)\n- LOT-126 (#217)\n- LOT-119 (#210)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ndependencies not done: LOT-044 (#70, in-progress), LOT-126 (#217), LOT-119 (#210)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #168\n- #117\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Verified on a device (BGTask simulated with the debugger command), result on the PR; no notification for an unknown/expired answer.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
